-- title:
--   Finiteness of level rings of the modular unit Δ(q)/Δ(qᵖ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` be the subfield of the field of Laurent series $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,(jq)$ for the divisors $d$ of $p$, and write $\mathrm{Afin}\ p$ for the subalgebra `chartAlg ℤ F {jFull p}` of $F$, the finite chart of the two-chart integral model attached to the element $jFull\ p = jq$ of $F$. Assume the Laurent series $\mathrm{modularUnitSeries}\ p = \Delta \cdot (\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p\,\Delta)^{-1}$, where $\Delta$ is $q$ times the $\eta$-product power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ`, lies in $F$. Let $v \in \mathrm{Afin}\ p$ be an element whose image in $F$ is either this series or $p^{12}$ times its inverse. Let $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ be monic with $\deg g \ge 1$ and $g(0) \neq 0$, and let $c$ be a nonzero integer with $g(0) \mid c$. Then the quotient of the localisation of $\mathrm{Afin}\ p$ away from the image of $c$ by the ideal generated by $g$ evaluated at the image of $v$, namely `levelRing p c v g`, is a finite module over $\mathbb{Z}$ localised away from $c$.
--
--   This is the finiteness assertion for the level sets of the modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ (and its Fricke transform $p^{12}\Delta(q^p)/\Delta(q)$) on the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of $X_0(p)$, over $\mathbb{Z}[1/c]$. It is the module-finiteness clause feeding into [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_self`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_self), where these level sets are exhibited as finite étale multisections.
